# Integration Testing

Purpose:
  Integration Testing

Skill: Integration Testing

ID:
  SKILL-CROSS-TEST-INTEGRATION

Domain:
  cross-cutting/testing

Use:
  testing component interactions

Apply:
  intermediate
  senior
  integration
  system-testing

Requires:
  testing-fundamentals
  testcontainers-or-mocks

Avoid:
  test-pollution
  external-dependency
  flaky-test
  testing-implementation

Level:
  L2

Status:
  STABLE

Maturity:
  MATURE

Risk:
  LOW

Review:
  2026-08

Version:
  1.0

EvidenceLevel:
  HIGH

SearchKeys:
  integration testing
  testcontainers
  component testing
  api testing

TechnologyLifecycle:
  Current: MATURE

HumanDoc:
  docs/skills/cross-cutting/testing/integration.md

Evidence:
  - Testcontainers Documentation
  - Integration Testing Guide
  - Production experience

Rules:
  [I1] Use real dependencies (test databases, services).
  [I2] Use Testcontainers for ephemeral environments.
  [I3] Clean up resources after each test.
  [I4] Tests MUST be idempotent.
  [I5] Use Docker Compose for multi-service setups.
  [I6] Mock only external third-party APIs.
  [I7] Set reasonable timeouts.
  [I8] Run integration tests in CI/CD.

Pros:
  - Higher confidence
  - Catches integration issues
  - Real scenarios

Cons:
  - Slower execution
  - Complex setup
  - Maintenance

Alternatives:
  - Contract testing
  - Component testing
  - E2E testing

State: +

